.TH CLIPNEST-GRANT-INPUT 8 "2026" "clipnest" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
clipnest-grant-input \- add the current user to the clipnest-input group
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pkexec clipnest-grant-input
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B clipnest-grant-input
is invoked only via
.BR pkexec (1),
gated by the
.B app.clipnest.grant-input
polkit action, itself only ever triggered from an explicit button in
Clipnest's own Settings \- never automatically, and never by the
.B clipnest
package's maintainer scripts.
.PP
It adds the user who authenticated the polkit prompt (identified via the
.B PKEXEC_UID
environment variable pkexec itself sets \- never a command-line argument)
to the
.B clipnest-input
system group. Membership in this dedicated group grants only the ability
to create a virtual input device via
.IR /dev/uinput ,
which Clipnest's auto-paste feature needs to synthesize a paste keystroke.
It does
.B not
grant read access to real keyboard/mouse input \- that would require the
.B input
group instead, which this package deliberately never uses (see
.IR /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/70-clipnest-uinput.rules ).
.PP
A re-login is required after running this before the new group membership
takes effect, since Linux group membership is resolved at login time.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR clipnest (1),
.BR pkexec (1)
